v0.5.0: sorted discovery, routed display names, models.dev param update via host RPC

Discovery results now sort by id, and ids carrying a vendor path
prefix (qwen/qwen-max) show their last segment as the display name
while the wire id stays whole. A new "update model info" action has
the browser send only the model ids (plus an optional proxy draft)
over the /llm-newapi connection RPC channel; the host half downloads
https://models.dev/api.json -- no cross-origin fetch in the browser,
and a plain HTTP forward proxy works because Node performs the
request -- and matches each id verbatim then by last path segment,
returning limit.context / limit.output. Ids matching several providers
(qwen vs alibaba) get a provider picker in the result panel; applying
offers overwrite or fill-blank modes, and unmatched ids keep their
values with a matched/unmatched count. The proxy toggle defaults to
off with http://127.0.0.1:7890 preset (7890/7897/10809 dropdown plus
custom input), persists with the settings section, is validated at
the write when enabled, and applies to that one download only.

typecheck, build, vitest 10/10, and smoke (registrations, discovery,
credentials, validation, ordering, display names, models.dev
matching) all green.
